# arch-ctm critical-review finding after merging develop into integrate/phase-ai-31-33
# MAJOR: scripts/phase-ai/run-hermes-graft-smoke.py issues acknowledge() as a fire-and-forget
# call and never verifies the ack round-trip actually completed before printing PASS --
# false-positive smoke evidence risk. File lives on develop (added at 0d0a5ebb) and is
# inherited into integrate/phase-ai-31-33 via the develop merge-forward at 7a02e7dd.
# PR #683, branch integrate/phase-ai-31-33 @ 7a02e7dd

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3133-HERMES-SMOKE-NO-ACK-VERIFY>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3133-HERMES-SMOKE-NO-ACK-VERIFY" ;
  triage:title "run-hermes-graft-smoke.py never verifies the ACK round-trip before reporting PASS" ;
  triage:description "Major: scripts/phase-ai/run-hermes-graft-smoke.py (present on develop since 0d0a5ebb 'test: add full Hermes graft smoke runner', inherited into integrate/phase-ai-31-33 unchanged via the develop merge-forward at 7a02e7dd). Lines 112-118 busy-poll receiver_session.read() in a `while time.monotonic() < deadline` loop (up to args.timeout, default 15s) to observe the sent marker message arriving -- this loop verifies message delivery/read only, not acknowledgement. At line 128, the script calls `receiver_session.acknowledge(message.message_id, f\"ack-{marker}\")` exactly once, with no retry, no return-value/state check, and no subsequent read/poll on the sender side (or any other channel) to confirm the sender actually observed the ack. Line 129 immediately prints `PASS acknowledge: message_id=...` based solely on the call not raising an exception -- a synchronous local API call succeeding does not establish that the ack round-trip to the peer/sender completed. The runner can therefore report smoke success (\"Hermes graft smoke test: PASS\", line 136) without any confirmation that the acknowledgement was actually received on the other end. This matches this project's known pattern of prior 'handwavey check' / false-PASS smoke findings (see AI-SMOKE-GATE-001 and related localhost false-PASS history) where local-only success signals were mistaken for end-to-end confirmation." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA-OBSERVABILITY-GAP" ;
  triage:severity "major" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-28T08:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:fixCommit "46d88bfe" ;
